Questionnaires built into Steady
--------------------------------
The questionnaire texts are not covered by Steady's licence; each stays under its own terms.

PHQ-9 (Patient Health Questionnaire-9) and GAD-7 (Generalized Anxiety Disorder-7)
  Developed by Drs Robert L. Spitzer, Janet B. W. Williams, Kurt Kroenke and colleagues, with an
  educational grant from Pfizer Inc. No permission is required to reproduce, translate, display or
  distribute them. https://www.phqscreeners.com/

PCL-5 (PTSD Checklist for DSM-5)
  Weathers, F. W., Litz, B. T., Keane, T. M., Palmieri, P. A., Marx, B. P., & Schnurr, P. P. (2013),
  US National Center for PTSD. In the public domain.
  https://www.ptsd.va.gov/professional/assessment/adult-sr/ptsd-checklist.asp

WHO-5 (WHO-Five Well-Being Index)
  World Health Organization, licensed CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO. Steady ships it marked "check licence",
  so each practice confirms its use before sending it. Steady does not use the WHO logo.
  https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/mental-health/who-5_english-original4da539d6ed4b49389e3afe47cda2326a.pdf

The breathing and grounding exercises and the thought record are OpenWorks IT's own wording of
widely used techniques (AGPL-3.0).

Questionnaires imported from the ReproSchema library, FHIR or JSON keep their own licences, which
Steady shows for each one.


